 ],
 "notes": "The default region (us-east-1) is not checked: candidates set it as a literal in the provider block, which is invisible in the plan. Per-AZ pairing (NAT gateway N in public subnet N, private route table N to NAT N, which public subnet and route table each one uses) is not expressible because subnet_id / nat_gateway_id are unknown at plan; counts and ref links are used instead. All stated CIDRs resolve against the default octets 10.0. Subnet-to-AZ pairing (a/b/c respectively) is checked with the prompt's default region us-east-1. Public-subnet association is checked as some association to a public subnet; that all three share the one route table holding the IGW route is not expressible (associations and routes reference the table separately)."
